module

public import EthLib.Cryptography.Hash.Keccak.Spec

/-!
# Keccak, fast form

The same functions as `EthLib.Cryptography.Hash.Keccak.keccakF` and `keccak256`, written so that a 32-bit target keeps all 25 lanes unboxed: the lanes are `UInt64` parameters and locals, each round is straight-line code, round constants are literals and every rotation is by a literal amount.

Generated by embedded/gen/keccak/gen.py and gen_i.py. `Keccak/FastProof.lean` proves `keccakF1 = keccakF` and `keccakF2 = keccakF` and installs `keccakF2` with `@[csimp]`; it also proves `padF msg = pad RATE msg` and a guarded in-place sponge `keccak256U = keccak256` (no longer installed). `Keccak/FastProofI.lean` proves the bit-interleaved sponge defined here: `keccak256I msg = keccak256 msg` whenever `(padF msg).size < USize.size`, and installs its guarded form `keccak256IG` (the body of `keccak256I` behind a `< 2^31 - 1` test, spec in the `else`) for `keccak256` with `@[csimp]`. The other sponges here (`keccak256F*`, `keccak256G*`), `keccakFU` and `keccakFI` are checked only by the differential test (outside this repository); they have no proof and no `@[csimp]`. (`absorbG` is not equal to `Internal.absorbBlocks` as stated: its `USize` index wraps for an array of `USize.size` bytes or more, which exists in the logic; `keccak256U` and `keccak256IG` add the guard.)

This docstring was edited by hand; regenerating the file with embedded/gen/keccak/gen.py overwrites it.
-/

@[expose] public section

